ForesightBench licensing
========================

ForesightBench combines two kinds of material, each under its own terms.

1. The dataset author's contribution

   The selection and decomposition of samples, the question framing, the
   record schema, the `asked`, `target` and `meta` annotations, the
   research-area tags and the documentation are copyright (c) 2026 Ruhaan
   Chopra and are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
   International license (CC BY 4.0):
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

2. Material from the source papers

   Every sample is built from one arXiv preprint, named by the sample's
   `arxiv_id`. The `prompt` adapts passages of that paper, keeping its
   technical details, equations and baseline numbers, and `title` is the
   paper's title. That material stays under the license its authors chose on
   arXiv, recorded for each sample in the `source_license` field:

   source_license                  license                                         papers  samples
   cc-by-4.0                       https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/         18      143
   cc-by-sa-4.0                    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/       2        7
   cc-by-nc-sa-4.0                 https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/    1        2
   cc-by-nc-nd-4.0                 https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/    1        1
   arxiv-nonexclusive-distrib-1.0  https://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/ 20      163

   Counts are over the 316-sample corpus. The 42-sample eval set has one
   sample per paper, so it carries every license in the table.

   If you use a sample, you are responsible for respecting its source license.
   Filter on `source_license == "cc-by-4.0"` to keep only material whose
   source is CC BY 4.0. The `baseline_value` and `method_value` fields are
   measurements reported by the source papers.

Removal requests

   If you are an author of a source paper and want its samples removed,
   email ruhaanchopra2005@gmail.com with the arXiv id.
